-- statement:
--   The frame matrix of the Eddington–Finkelstein metric $g^{\rm EF}_{M,\varepsilon}$, with $f=1-2M/r$: $$\mathrm{frame}(x)=\begin{pmatrix}1&1&0&0\\\varepsilon\tfrac{f-1}{2}&\varepsilon\tfrac{f+1}{2}&0&0\\0&0&1/r&0\\0&0&0&1/(r\sin\theta)\end{pmatrix}$$ (`frameE` as a function of indices, `frame` as a matrix), which satisfies $\mathrm{frame}^{\mathsf T}g^{\rm EF}\,\mathrm{frame}=\mathrm{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ on $U^{\rm EF}$ when $\varepsilon^2=1$; it contains no square root of $f$, hence is valid at $r=2M$.
